[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="StoryText" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://core/data/story_text.gd" id="1_st0ry"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_st0ry")
awakening_lines = Array[String](["Where... where is this? I can smell wet leaves, and my head feels as if someone has packed it with wool.", "I keep reaching for my name, and it isn't there. Neither is how I came to be here. There's nothing at all, like a room that somebody has emptied.", "I ought to try standing up, though my legs don't seem to agree, and I ache in places I couldn't even put a name to."])
beefcake_npc_intro_lines = Array[String](["STOP RIGHT THERE! NOBODY CROSSES THE GORGE WITHOUT A SPOTTER, AND I AM THE SPOTTER, AND I AM NOT SPOTTING ANYBODY ACROSS IT TODAY!","THE BRIDGE STAYS UP BY ORDER OF CHANCELLOR CLENCH, BECAUSE ONLY IRON MATTERS! IRON AND HYDRATION! (quieter) The regime is very big on hydration, so do drink something while you're waiting.","IF YOU WANT THIS CRANK YOU WILL HAVE TO EARN IT, TEN REPS AND NO REST! I HAVE NOT SAT DOWN SINCE SPRING AND I FEEL FANTASTIC! ...I THINK IT IS FANTASTIC. MY KNEES STOPPED TELLING ME THINGS."])
beefcake_npc_victory_lines = Array[String](["...Oh, no. Was I yelling just then? I was, wasn't I. I'm so sorry. That was the pre-workout talking, and once it starts it doesn't know how to stop.","Chancellor Clench had Grandmaster Flex locked away under the House of Gains, ten years ago now. People still whisper that the old man never broke. I wish I'd whispered with them, instead of standing out here yelling.","The bridge is yours, friend. Do stretch before you cross, though. A pulled hamstring is a terrible thing to bring home from a trip."])
beefcake_npc_defeat_lines = Array[String](["HA! THE PUMP IS STILL MINE! GO HOME AND HYDRATE! THAT IS AN ORDER, NOT CONCERN! ...IT IS A LITTLE BIT CONCERN.","COME BACK WHEN YOU CAN LIFT, AND I WILL BE RIGHT HERE, BECAUSE THE BRIDGE STAYS UP AND SO DO I! NEITHER OF US HAS BEEN ALLOWED TO SIT DOWN IN A VERY LONG TIME!"])
gourmand_npc_intro_lines = Array[String](["TASTE IT! The Special Sauce is in everything now - my soup, my tea, my very SOUL - and isn't it WONDERFUL?","The pantry is closed by order of the Grand Chef herself, and the key stays right here on my apron. It's all for the war effort!","So if it's the key you're after, you will have to win it from me in a duel, here and now, with the whole pantry watching! Yes, Chef! No - YOU, Chef!"])
gourmand_npc_victory_lines = Array[String](["Oh... the sauce has let go of me. Is that plain bread? With nothing on it at all? I could weep. In fact I am weeping, and I don't mind who sees.","The Grand Chef stopped tasting her own sauces years ago, and the Chef I trained under ALWAYS tasted. It's the same face and the same apron... so who has been wearing them?","Whatever has gone wrong here starts in the Test Kitchen, at the far end of the Buffet, and it was never built for casseroles. Take a biscuit for the road. No, take two."])
gourmand_npc_defeat_lines = Array[String](["Under-seasoned, the whole performance, from your first card to your last! NEXT!","The pantry door stays shut and the key stays on my apron. Go and simmer for a while, and come back whenever you like - I shall be right here, stirring!"])
refusemancer_npc_intro_lines = Array[String](["...the green is hungry... the green is HUNGRY... nothing goes to waste...","...this path belongs to the Rotheart now... turn back... before the green decides you would make good compost...","...if you won't leave, the green will keep you... it keeps everything now... nothing it holds is ever allowed to go..."])
refusemancer_npc_victory_lines = Array[String](["Oh, no. Did I thorn at you? I'm so sorry. The Rot talks very softly inside your head, right up until the moment it's doing all the talking.","The Rot took Archdruid Compostella first, down at the Rotheart, in the deepest part of the Verdant Dump, and everything grew outward from there. It got into me the day a very tidy lady with shears came calling.","The path is clear now. Go gently in there, and if you meet a raccoon, say hello to him from me. They're very good boys, whatever anybody tells you."])
refusemancer_npc_defeat_lines = Array[String](["...the green is patient... nothing ends here any more... come back when you're ready to stay...","...come back... the green can wait... it has forgotten how to do anything else..."])
necrocrat_npc_intro_lines = Array[String](["Halt. Passage through this checkpoint requires a permit, and I regret to inform you that no permit has ever been issued. You may take a number while you wait.","Your number is zero, as is everyone's. This checkpoint is now serving nobody, and will continue to do so.","The authorization is valid, and policy states that I must stop you. I have read the whole of the policy, twice, and nowhere does it say why."])
necrocrat_npc_victory_lines = Array[String](["...I can hear my own thoughts again. I believe I have been Pending for ten years. It was very quiet in there, and very orderly, and none of it was me.","{villain} never had to corrupt us. He used our own rules against us: a perfectly valid transfer of authority, notarized and filed. We stamped it ourselves.","The Hall of Final Approvals is at the top of the D.N.A., and whoever sits in it holds the authorization. Go carefully. Or fill out a form first. Ideally, do both."])
necrocrat_npc_defeat_lines = Array[String](["Your application has been denied. You may reapply in ten to twelve centuries, which I am required to tell you is our express service.","Not today, then. You are welcome to take another number and try again, though I should mention that it will also be zero."])
equipment_vendor_intro_lines = Array[String](["Security Protocol One requires me to assess every customer's gait before they reach the counter. Yours is adequate, so you may approach at your current level of walking.", "I am Bertram Beetsworth, Assistant TO the Regional Merchant. The TO is load-bearing, and I would thank you not to drop it.", "Everything on this rack is inventoried and oiled under Security Protocol Seven, which is strictly need-to-know, and I have checked the list and you do not need to know.", "Please do not reach for the drawer, because its contents are classified, and as of this moment so is your interest in them."])
equipment_vendor_return_lines = Array[String](["Fact: a return customer strengthens the economy and also my employee-of-the-month case file, so I would ask you to look satisfied for the record.", "Fact: the beets came in early this year, and the bear has been informed. We have an understanding, in which I do not ask why it is here and it does not ask about the beets."])
graveyard_intro_lines = Array[String](["The stones here were stacked by hands that stopped moving a long time ago.", "Something under the cairn is still keeping count of its turns. It has been keeping count since before {villain} came.", "Touch it, and it will not stop counting until one of you does."])
graveyard_victory_lines = Array[String](["The counting stops. For now.", "Whatever was keeping time down there has nothing left to spend it on.", "The stones are just stones again. Take what it was guarding."])
graveyard_defeat_lines = Array[String](["It is still counting.", "Come back when you have more turns to spare than it does."])
quest_dialogue = {}
texts = {
"still.wake": ["You wake in a forest clearing with leaves in your hair, and no idea how long you have been lying there.", "A faint glow of four colors is fading from your hand, like a thought you almost had.", "Someone in a hood is kneeling beside you, shaking your shoulder gently, then less gently. Their face stays in shadow."],
"still.flex": ["Grandmaster Flex walks into the throne room in his prison rags, and the whole hall falls silent.", "He breathes in, slow and even. Ten years without iron have worn him thin as wire, but he stands perfectly straight.", "Across the room, the ruler of the House of Gains takes one step back."],
"still.doppel": ["You watch the chef's perfect smile slip away with her face.", "Beneath it there is only a shifting shadow in a spotless white coat.", "Behind the shadow, the unfinished war machines stand in their rows and do not move."],
"still.approval": ["You hear the great DENIED stamp crack. For the first time in the Department's long afterlife, it does not come down.", "Forms rise around you. Across the Department, a thousand clerks look up from their desks.", "Somewhere nearby, you hear a pen stop scratching."],
"still.rotheart": ["Light pours through the splitting Rotheart.", "Before you, the purple vines wither. At the heart of the wound, the Archdruid kneels, free and breathing.", "Wildflowers follow the light outward, field by field, through the Dump."],
"still.primm": ["The mirrors crack one by one, and for the first time in ten years {villain} sees himself in them.", "There is no crown and no perfect smile, only a tired man kneeling above a very small kingdom.", "Light pours in through the broken glass. It does not feel like winning. It feels like the end of a long, quiet lie."],
"still.reunion": ["In the Capital's square the leaders of the four Paths clasp hands, and several people in the crowd begin to cry.", "Four banners fly from the same pole. It is a little crowded, and nobody minds.", "At the edge of the crowd you catch yourself looking for a hood with leaves caught in it, and not finding one. Not yet."],
"start.gate_title": ["The Forgotten Cave"],
"start.gate_prompt": ["A cold draft rises out of the dark, and it smells of old stone and older water. The stranger said the town lies on the other side of this cave. Go in?"],
"prologue.rescuer.1": ["Easy, now. Stay down for a moment and get your breath back. After what they put you through, I'm amazed you're breathing at all.", "Keep your voice low, though. We aren't the only ones in these woods tonight, and the others aren't looking for you out of kindness."],
"prologue.wanderer.1": ["I don't know this place. I don't even know my own name. ...Who are you?"],
"prologue.rescuer.2": ["A friend. I know that isn't much of an answer, and I'm sorry. It's the only one I can give you tonight.", "Can you still draw on the Paths? Hold out your hand and let me see. Gently, I only want to look."],
"prologue.wanderer.2": ["...I can feel them. All four of them, but faintly, like voices through a wall."],
"prologue.rescuer.3": ["Then they didn't manage to take everything. That will have to do for now, because the Path-ologists are already out hunting for us.", "Tell me: which Path resonates within you?"],
"prologue.rescuer.4": ["That one, then. Hold on to it as tightly as you can. The others will come back to you in time; I'm almost sure of it.", "The Forgotten Cave behind me is your escape. It comes out at {town}, and Elder Maren will be waiting for you there. Find her first.", "Do you hear that? They're close, but they don't know about the cave. Hardly anyone remembers it's here any more.", "Go now, and don't stop for anything. I'll draw them off the other way, and once I'm clear of them, I'll find you. I always do."],
"prologue.wanderer.3": ["She's gone, and the shouting has gone after her. I don't know who those people are, but I'd rather not be standing here when they come back."],
"prologue.self_talk": ["The trees are packed too tightly to squeeze through here. It will have to be the cave, then.", "There's no sense in getting lost twice in one day. I'll go back up the path to the glowing arch.", "Whatever is waiting for me, it's on the other side of that cave.", "She said someone would be waiting on the other side, whoever she was. And whatever is in that cave, it can't be worse than those Path-ologists."],
"memory.title_format": ["Fragment %d of 4: %s"],
"memory.hint": ["E / click: continue"],
"memory.1.title": ["Warmth"],
"memory.1.intro": ["You've gone as pale as flour. Sit down, sit down. Something has come back to you, hasn't it?", "Tell me all of it, however small it seems to you. In my experience it's the small things that turn out to matter."],
"memory.1.fragment": ["There is light, four colors of it, as warm as bathwater, spilling across a ceiling I can't quite see.", "A woman is humming a tune with no words to it, and it rises and falls like someone breathing in their sleep.", "A hand rests on my head, gentle and certain, and it smells of lavender and woodsmoke.", "Then the light thins, like breath on glass, and I am back beside the fire."],
"memory.1.after": ["...A lullaby. That tune comes from the old days, from the court, and there are very few of us left who would know it. Fewer still who ever hummed it to a child.", "Have some pie. And don't ask me why my eyes are wet, because I shan't tell you, and you wouldn't want to make an old tortoise lie.", "But look at you. With one zone free, the corruption is losing its grip on the land, and it's slipping off you along with it.", "You ought to be able to carry a second Path now. Go down to the Deck Station and try building a deck with two, and then come and tell me how it feels."],
"memory.1.announce_title": ["A Second Path Opens"],
"memory.1.announce_body": ["With the first zone free, the corruption smothering your gift has weakened. Your decks may now use two Paths, and dual-Path cards can finally be played."],
"memory.1.announce_line": ["Decks may now use two Paths."],
"memory.2.title": ["The Cells"],
"memory.2.intro": ["Another one, is it? No, don't hide behind your teacup, dearie. Put it down and tell me."],
"memory.2.fragment": ["White rooms, and a white light that never changes, whatever the hour is outside.", "There is glass on every side of me, and behind the glass there are faces in white coats, taking notes.", "No one in that place ever uses my name. They call me 'the Subject', and whatever I do, the only thing they ever say to me is 'again.'", "Again. Again. Again.", "I wasn't lost. I was kept."],
"memory.2.after": ["Glass, and white coats, and 'again.' So that is where they had you, all those years.", "You've earned some truth from me in return, so here is the first piece of it: I'm not only an old tortoise who bakes.", "There's a resistance in this kingdom, and I'm its contact here in {town}. A woman called Wren leads it, from a hideout inside the Capital itself.", "I wasn't sure of you before, and I'm sorry for that. I'm sure of you now, or near enough, and there aren't many people I would say that about."],
"memory.3.title": ["The Coup"],
"memory.3.intro": ["You're shaking like a leaf. Sit down, slowly now, there's no hurry. Here, take hold of my hand."],
"memory.3.fragment": ["A throne room at night, with the candles guttering under banners that have four colors woven into one.", "A man in white and gold kneels before the king and speaks to him in a soft voice. Then he rises, and that soft voice is the last soft thing in the room.", "Two pairs of hands are on my shoulders, pushing me behind them, back toward the dark.", "I know that man's face. I think I have always known it. {villain}."],
"memory.3.after": ["A man in white and gold, who knelt and then stood up. And before that, those rooms of yours with glass on every side.", "I know that glass, because I helped to blow it. A long time ago I founded the study of the Paths, and I did it for the best of reasons, the way people generally do.", "{villain} took my work and built a cage out of it, and the best student I ever had stayed on to run the laboratory for him. And I ran away.", "I have been hiding here ever since with my hands in pie dough, where nobody would think to ask what else those hands had made.", "That's my secret, and now you're holding it, the same way I have been holding yours. You may do with it as you see fit."],
"memory.4.title": ["A Name"],
"memory.4.intro": ["There's something in your face today. You look like somebody who has just been handed a key. Come and sit, and tell me what it opens."],
"memory.4.fragment": ["A boy of eleven stands in a coat too fine for the cold, and someone is calling to him across a courtyard: '{prince}!'", "I turn toward a woman's voice, and then a man's, and on every door around me is the {royal_house} crest: four signs in a ring.", "{prince_full}, son of the king and queen. The whole kingdom believes he died ten years ago.", "That is who I am."],
"memory.4.after": ["{prince}. {prince} {royal_house}. I met a boy at court once, hiding behind his mother's cloak, and he asked me why tortoises carry their houses about with them.", "I told him, 'So that we are never far from home.'", "I knew, you see. The Warden opens that tunnel for one family only, and I knew who you were the moment you walked out of it. I was too frightened to say so.", "Four signs in a ring, the same as the ones carved on this stick of mine. I have leaned on it for ten years and never told a soul why.", "And my laboratory, my life's work, was used on that boy. It was used on you. Forgive me, if you ever can. I would understand it if you couldn't."],
"memory.4.reply": ["My mother called to me across that courtyard. I can hear her voice now, and I still can't see her face. I'd like to, one day. I'd like to know what the two of them were like.", "You built the glass, Maren. You also gave me a bed and a pie when you still thought I might be a spy. I know which of those I'm keeping."],
"memory.4.after2": ["...Then let us make this kingdom a home again, {prince}. All of it, for all of them."],
"memory.4.intro_known": ["You have the look of someone who has just been told a thing he didn't want to hear. Was it {villain} who told you?", "Sit down, and tell me what he said to you. All of it, even the parts you would sooner not say aloud."],
"memory.4.after_known": ["So he knew you from the very first. He told you who you are, and now you've come to me for the rest of it.", "I knew as well. The Warden opens that tunnel for one family only, and I knew who you were the moment you came out of it. I was simply too frightened to say so.", "So hear it from somebody who held your hand at court: you are {prince_full}, and I am so very sorry for what was done to you with the things I built."],
"town.elder.stage.0": ["I still don't know what to make of you, dearie. But you need feeding a good deal more than you need questioning, so sit yourself down for a minute.","Have as much pie as you like. Just keep your eyes off the recipe card. Better people than you have tried for it, and I caught every one of them."],
"town.elder.stage.1": ["That tune has stayed with you, hasn't it? I can see it in your face. Good. Keep it somewhere safe, dearie, even on the days when it hurts to hear.","Have you found any more answers out there? I keep telling myself it's none of my business, and then I keep asking anyway."],
"town.elder.stage.2": ["Somebody on the square says you've a look of the old court about you. 'That's no prince,' I told them. 'That's a damp young man with good posture.' Oh, don't look so startled, dearie.","When you find Wren in the Capital, tell her my pie is still the best thing in this kingdom. She'll argue with you, and she'll be wrong, and it'll do her good to hear it all the same."],
"town.elder.stage.3": ["Well, I've told you the worst of me now. Whatever else I have to say to you will come easily, after that.","Go on, dearie. That last road won't open by itself, and if it were left to me to walk there, the regime would die of old age first."],
"town.elder.stage.4": ["{prince}. I keep wanting to curtsy when you come in, and my knees keep voting against it.", "Go on, then. The kingdom has waited ten years for you and can manage one more hour, but this pie won't keep for ten minutes."],
"town.elder.known_early": ["{prince}. So {villain} let it slip, did he, the smug creature. I had hoped you would hear it from me, in a warm kitchen, and not from him.", "Sit down. The rest of your memories will come when they're ready, and I'll be right here when they do, with a pie in the oven. I'm not going anywhere."],
"tutorial.warden.before": ["...Footsteps. It has been a long time since anything came down here to wake me.", "No one has walked this way since the house above fell silent. I have kept the door all the same, for there was no one left to tell me that I might stop.", "Turn back, traveller. Only one may pass this door, and he is long dead."],
"tutorial.warden.after": ["...The door knows your hand. I do not understand how that can be, but I was not left here to understand. Pass, and may the Paths guide you home.", "The light goes out of the Warden's eyes slowly, like a lamp turned down for the night by someone who means to come back to it."],
"cave_mouth.maren": ["Hmph. About time. {villain}'s soldiers have been up and down that road all day, and nobody has come out of this cave in ten years, so you'll have to forgive an old tortoise for staring.", "And just look at the state of you. I told her I would help whoever she sent along, but I don't recall agreeing to take in a half-drowned stray who can barely stand.", "I didn't want any part of this, and I told her so to her face. She went and did it anyway. She always does, that one.", "Still, you need a bed, and I've gone and baked far too much pie again, so I can hardly leave you standing out here on your own, can I?"],
"cave_mouth.wanderer": ["I'm sorry to be a trouble. I don't know who I am, or where this is. I don't even know the name of the woman who got me out."],
"cave_mouth.maren_end": ["Hm. If she didn't give you her name, she'll have had her reasons, and I won't be the one to spoil them. As for where you are, this is {town}. We settle most things here with cards, and I see you've brought a deck.", "If your memory really is gone, you'll be with us a while, so you'd best get to know people. Go and say hello to Sable, Tilly and Pip on the square, buy yourself a card from Sable, and then come back to me."],
"start.tunnel": ["There is a narrow gap in the old treeline here. It would be easy to miss, and easy enough to slip through, if you aren't afraid of a shortcut."],
"town.name": ["{town}"],
"town.elder.first": ["Up and walking, I see. Good. I'm Elder Maren, dearie, and this is {town}, where the four Paths used to meet, and argue, and borrow each other's pans and never give them back.","Ten years ago {kingdom} was whole. Beefcakes kept the lights on, Gourmands fed us, Necrocrats minded the dead, Refusemancers turned rubbish into harvests. Four peoples who never matched, stitched together, and it held.","Then {villain}, the Minister of Improvements, took the Paths one at a time and set his own people over them. Now every road out of town has a gatekeeper across it: a bridge, a barrier, a pantry door and a wall of thorns.","Beat a road's gatekeeper and that road opens. Before you try, buy a few cards from Sable and sort your deck out at the Deck Station. Then come back to me for pie. Pie, mind you, and not answers. I'm short of those."],
"town.elder.return": ["There are four roads out of town, dearie: the Gainlands, the Buffet, the D.N.A. and the Dump. Pick one and see it through to the end before you start on the next.","For all I know you're somebody's spy, and here I am feeding you. I've been wrong about people before, you see, and it cost more than I like to think about."],
"town.elder.idle": ["Still here, dearie? {villain} would like nothing better than you sat by my fire for good, so let's not oblige him. Besides, you're in my chair.","The pie on the sill wants another hour, dearie, and you don't. Off you go, and it'll be ready when you're back.","If it's advice you're after, eat something. And if you were hoping for better advice than that, eat something else as well.","I've told you all I can for now, dearie. The rest you'll have to go out and find for yourself, and I'd only slow you down.","Mind the fountain as you go, dearie. People throw their wishes into it, and over the years a good many of them have been mine.","Off you go, dearie. I'll be right here when you get back. We tortoises are very dependable, so long as nobody's in a hurry."],
"town.elder.idle.1": ["One zone free, and you're back for pie already. Very well, but it's one slice a zone from now on, dearie. I've only just made that rule.", "Three roads are still shut. I'd go and see to them myself, dearie, but at my pace I would get there some time next spring.", "The square was singing last night. It was dreadful, and the best thing I've heard in ten years. Don't you dare tell them so."],
"town.elder.idle.2": ["Two zones free, and the square is louder for it. I complain about the noise every morning, and I don't mean a word.", "That's halfway, dearie. I'd tell you I was proud of you, but then you might stop trying, and we can't have that.", "Auntie Alembic keeps asking after you. I tell her you're busy, and for once in my life it's even true."],
"town.elder.idle.3": ["One Path left under {villain}'s thumb, and the whole town is holding its breath. I can hold mine for a week, being a tortoise. They can't.", "Three zones free, dearie. Do try to finish the fourth before this pie goes stale. I'd give it about a week.", "You walk like somebody with somewhere to be, these days. I think I liked the damp young man better. He came to see me more often."],
"town.elder.idle.4": ["All four Paths free, and {villain} still sat up in his castle as though nothing had changed. Go and knock, dearie, and knock loudly.", "The roads are open again, and even I've been out on them. I passed a hare this morning, and he has asked for a recount.", "Eat something first, and then go to the castle. Nobody ever toppled a tyrant properly on an empty stomach."],
"town.elder.progress.1": ["One zone free. Hm. And the old cottage at the end of Champions' Road has started cheering at night, from somewhere down in its cellar. I've decided I would rather not ask."],
"town.elder.progress.2": ["Two zones free, and Auntie Alembic has opened the Alchemist's on the square. She brews cards from two Paths at once, if you can stand all the steam.","She's been asking for your leftovers, too. Coming from her, that's a compliment."],
"town.elder.progress.3": ["Three zones free. There's only one Path left under {villain}'s thumb now, and I won't tell you what I'm feeling about that, except that it's a great deal."],
"town.elder.progress.4": ["All four Paths are free, and {kingdom} is whole again, or very nearly. Up in his castle, {villain} will be counting what he has left.", "Get some rest tonight. Then we finish this, you and I and everybody else, together."],
"town.guard": ["Hm. You came back. Wrote it in the notebook: 'came back.' Best two words I know.","Gate stays open. Always has. My girl's still up that road somewhere, and I'd hate for her to come home one night and find it shut."],
"town.guard.capital_offer": ["Hm. That road goes to the Capital. You'll be wanting to know why nobody comes back from it.", "Four Paths kept that city alive. Beefcakes ran the lights, Gourmands the kitchens, Necrocrats the graveyards, Refusemancers the bins. Then {villain} put all four in chains.", "So now it's Blackout, Famine, Restless Dead and Clutter up there. Dark streets, slow legs, no food that heals, rubbish in your deck.", "You could walk in today, but you wouldn't get far. Free the four zones first. Each one you free turns one of those services back on.", "My girl Isla went up that road eight years ago. If you see her up there... tell her the gate is still open."],
"town.guard.capital_active": ["Hm. Services still broken up there. The board by the road keeps count, if you want to check.", "Hm. Each zone you free turns a service back on, and the castle gets a little less frightening. Can't say the same for my knees."],
"town.guard.capital_done": ["Hm. All four zones free. The lights are on up there. I can see them from here.", "Go on, knock on that castle door, and knock hard. And if you see Isla up there... tell her I'm still watching the road."],
"capital.castle.warning": ["The castle door is cold to the touch. With the city's services still broken, whatever waits inside will have every advantage.", "You could go in now. It would be wiser to wait until the city is back on its feet."],
"gate.beefcake.freed": ["You really did it. Grandmaster Flex is out! The first thing he did was make me stretch for forty minutes, and I cried twice, but they were the good kind of tears.","The bridge stays down for good now, though I still come out and oil the crank every morning. Looking after it is how I say sorry, and I've a lot of sorry left to get through.","Would you like to spar? Gently, I mean, and I'll spot you. I'm still a spotter, only now I get to say it at an ordinary volume, and honestly that's a huge relief."],
"gate.necrocrat.freed": ["The afterlife is processing again. Agnes says the queue moved four whole numbers yesterday, so we had cake to mark the occasion.","I have a new stamp now, and it says HELPED. I've used it nine times so far, and yes, I am keeping count.","You may challenge me again if you'd like to, and you won't need a permit for it. That's my favourite rule. I wrote it myself."],
"gate.gourmand.freed": ["She's back, the real Grand Chef. She tasted my soup, frowned at it and said 'more salt', and I don't believe I have ever been so happy in my life.","The pantry door stays wide open now, and people wander in for biscuits all day long. I keep a tin by the hinge for them.","Do you fancy a friendly duel, for old times' sake? The loser washes the ladle, and I ought to warn you that it's a very big ladle."],
"gate.refusemancer.freed": ["Archdruid Compostella is herself again, and she hugged me! She smells of rain, and a little bit of compost, which is exactly how an Archdruid ought to smell.","Most of the thorns have gone. I've kept one in a pot, and it's behaving itself, but I'm not ready to let it anywhere near the curtains.","Would you like a practice round? I'll try very hard not to thorn at you. The raccoons have come to watch, so we had both better be on our best behaviour."],
"gate.beefcake.blocked": ["The bridge is drawn up on the far side of the gorge. Somebody very large is standing by the crank over there, shouting about hydration."],
"gate.beefcake.cleared": ["Brick Bronson cracks his knuckles, takes hold of the crank with one hand and lowers the bridge, glancing over his shoulder to make sure you're watching.", "The planks thump down across the gorge, and the road into the Gainlands lies open."],
"gate.necrocrat.blocked": ["The barrier is down, and a stamped sign beside it says the road needs a permit. Nobody has ever been issued one."],
"gate.necrocrat.cleared": ["Prudence Pallor stamps a permit, hands it over, and files the original in triplicate.", "The barrier creaks up, and the road to the D.N.A. is open."],
"gate.gourmand.blocked": ["An enormous pantry door blocks the lane, locked tight, with a keyhole the size of a dinner plate."],
"gate.gourmand.cleared": ["Chef Fennel Gravois hands over a key the size of a ladle, and it turns in the lock with a satisfying clunk.", "The great pantry door swings open on a smell of roasting meat and fresh bread, and underneath it, faintly, the smell of hot iron."],
"gate.refusemancer.blocked": ["A wall of thorns has swallowed the forest path, and it rises and falls slowly, as if it were breathing."],
"gate.refusemancer.cleared": ["Moss Mulligan lays a hand on the thorns, and they sigh, turn brown and crumble into leaf mould.", "The forest path to the Verdant Dump is open."],
"town.vendor.first": ["Well met, {wanderer}. I'm Sable, darling, and I sell cards, and I throw in the stories about them for nothing, because a card without its story is only stiff paper.","That starter deck of yours is half plain neutral cards, darling: honest, dependable and a little dull. The power is in the Paths, all four of them, so buy a few and put them to work at the Deck Station.","And where do my cards come from? The past, darling, like everything worth having, and that's all you'll get. My prices are fair, more or less, which is more than I can say for {villain}'s taxes on them."],
"town.vendor.return": ["Back again, darling? Every card on this table is honest, I promise you, and the misprints have simply led a more adventurous life with their spelling than the rest of us."],
"town.item_vendor.first": ["Hello, you look like you need supplies and I've got so many, I'm Tilly Tonic, and I'm teal today, which is good news, because teal means the new batch works!","Everything here is one use in a fight, so you equip what you buy on your Character screen, and then you use it on your turn, and then it's gone and you come back and see me.","Probably don't use them on yourself, though, unless it's a healing one, because I tested the healing one and I'm fine, I went green, but I'm usually green so that hardly counts."],
"town.item_vendor.gift": ["Your first visit gets a freebie, and it's Power Wraps! You wrap a unit and it gets tougher for the whole fight, and I wrapped my own arm once to test them and it's still tough, and also still a bit stuck.","Here's how you get them ready: press C, or go to Menu and then Character, and find Items, which is the big shiny panel, and I promise you can't miss it.","Click the Power Wraps and then click an empty slot, and that's all there is to it. A slotted item is ready in every fight until it's used up.","It's one wrap and one use and then it's gone, but there are more on my shelf, and look, I've gone green again, and green means business is good."],
"town.item_vendor.gift_waiting": ["Did you equip the Power Wraps yet? It's press C, then Items, then click the wraps and then an empty slot, and I'm only asking because I can't see them on you.","I'll wait right here, I don't mind a bit, except that I'm very bad at waiting and I think I'm starting to turn yellow."],
"town.item_vendor.return": ["You're back for more potions, oh good, just remember to equip them on your Character screen before a fight, and maybe skip the orange one until I've stopped matching it."],
"storeroom.locked": ["The door is cold to the touch, colder than the evening. Behind it, several voices are whispering the same word over and over, just too low to make out.", "Someone painted a ring of small symbols round the frame a long time ago, and someone else has tried very hard to scrub them off."],
"storeroom.before": ["Who is that, opening the Tonic door? Nobody opens the Tonic door, because the Tonics made very sure, a long time ago, that nobody would.", "There were three of us, once, and a lantern, and a lady in this room who promised it would show us the ones we'd lost. Tilly's great-grandmother. She had such kind hands.", "The lantern showed us something, but it wasn't who we'd lost. And afterwards, the door wouldn't open from this side any more."],
"storeroom.wanderer": ["...Tilly sells bandages and tonics. What was her great-grandmother selling?"],
"storeroom.challenge": ["Remedies, she called them. The chalk is still under the floorboards if you know where to scratch, and the jars on the top shelf were never for coughs.", "We won't be bargained with and we won't be prayed at. But a game, a fair one, with every card on the table... she always did love her games. Win, and perhaps we'll finally be let go."],
"storeroom.after_win": ["...Oh. That's the first fair thing to happen in this room in ninety years.", "We can feel the door now, both sides of it. We're going, before whatever she tied us to notices that the knot has come loose.", "The lantern is on the top shelf. Don't light it. Tell Tilly she can keep the shop, but she should burn the ledger under the third floorboard, and she shouldn't read it first."],
"storeroom.after_loss": ["That wasn't enough, and it wasn't nearly enough to loosen what she tied. Go away and come back stronger, and please don't stand so close to the chalk."],
"storeroom.cleared": ["Just shelves now, and warmer than it's been in years. On the top shelf sits an unlit lantern with soot on the inside of the glass."],
"town.equipment_vendor.too_early": ["Halt, please. Under Security Protocol Two, equipment is issued on referral only, and in this town it is Elder Maren who does the referring.", "Come back when you have Elder Maren's blessing. Better posture is always appreciated, but I regret that it cannot be accepted in its place."],
"quest.armory.start": ["Elder Maren sent you, which I could tell from your gait, because it now says 'referred'. Congratulations: your file is finally thick enough to be called a file.", "Before I am permitted to issue gear, protocol requires exactly one thing of you, which is that you win a fight. Any fight counts, and I will know if you lie to me about it.", "Fact: there are things roaming the outskirts, on the lanes round the edge of town. They are rude and they are close, and not one of them is on my referral list.", "Beat one of them and then come back to me, and I will hand you something pointy."],
"quest.armory.waiting": ["The whole requirement is one fight won, and so far I count zero. I should mention that I am very good at counting to zero.", "Security Protocol Four: check the outskirts. Enemies roam the lanes round the edge of town, and any win counts.", "I will be here in the meantime, guarding the drawer. The drawer does not know that it is being guarded, and that is the whole point."],
"quest.armory.equip": ["Security Protocol Nine: gear in a bag protects nobody, so please equip it.","Press C, click the Weapon slot on the figure, choose the blade and press Equip. That is four steps, and I have written them down for you, in my head.","Please be aware that unequipped gear will be noted in your file, and that your file is already very thick."],
"quest.armory.equip_waiting": ["The blade is still in the bag. I can see the bag from here, and I have reason to believe that the bag can see me.","Menu, then Character, then the Weapon slot, then Equip. Security Protocol Nine does not repeat itself, so I am repeating it for you as a personal courtesy."],
"quest.armory.done": ["That is one fight, won, and so I will now stamp your file three times, because three is the correct number of stamps. Stamp. Stamp. Stamp.", "Security Protocol Twelve: report to Elder Maren when we are finished here, because she is the one who decides where things get pointed.", "Here is your Starter Blade. With it, the first unit you play each battle hits a little harder. Protocol also requires me to say: do not run with it.", "All five equipment slots are yours as of now, and for the record they are helm, weapon, armor, boots and relic.", "The good stuff is rarer, and protocol says you can only wear so much of it until you level up. Fact: bears do not wear helms, and I have come to suspect that bears are wiser than us."],
"town.hidden_vendor": ["You found the chest, so I suppose you've earned a look. Epic and Legendary goods, quiet prices.","{villain}'s tax collectors don't know this stall exists. Let's keep it that way. Shh."],
"town.arena.name": ["The Undercroft"],
"town.arena.locked": ["There's a cellar hatch beside the old cottage, chained shut, and someone has scratched two little crossed swords into the wood.", "Somewhere below, very faintly, someone is rehearsing the word CHAMPION over and over. It seems he isn't ready for you yet."],
"town.arena.announce": ["The word around the square is that the abandoned cottage at the end of Champions' Road has started roaring at night.", "It's coming from the cellar, they say, and somebody brave ought to go and check the hatch. Somebody like you, perhaps."],
"town.arena.intro": ["WELCOME TO THE UNDERCROFT, CHAMPION! I AM ANNOUNCER GRAND BELLOWS, KEEPER OF THE SAND! (normal voice) Mind the third stair, won't you? It's loose, and I think it holds a grudge.", "FOR A THOUSAND YEARS THE FOUR PATHS SETTLED THEIR RIVALRIES IN THE OLD ARENA! (normal voice) Then {villain} chained the doors, which seemed a shame, so a few of us came down here. SO WE DUG.", "SINCE YOU FREED A ZONE, THE RING IS OPEN! (normal voice) It's battles and puzzles, tiers one to three, and there are prizes for you: ring-exclusive gear, gold and essence.", "FIRST CLEARS PAY OUT, AND REPEATS ARE FOR GLORY! (normal voice) And for snacks, I should say. I brought snacks, and there are plenty to go round."],
"town.arena.return": ["THE SAND IS HOT AND THE CEILING IS LOW! (normal voice) Pick a fight whenever you like, champion. The crowd is mostly my echo, I'm afraid, but he's very loyal and he agrees with EVERYTHING."],
"town.alchemist.name": ["Auntie Alembic's"],
"town.alchemist.locked": ["The door of Auntie Alembic's is bolted, and a note is pinned to it in green ink, in what looks like four different handwritings at once:", "'CLOSED UNTIL TWO ZONES ARE FREE. {villain} TOOK MY CAULDRON. I AM BREWING IN THE SINK. THE SINK IS COPING. - A.'"],
"town.alchemist.announce": ["With two zones free, a cauldron bubbles to life in {town}, and Auntie Alembic's is open! Bring your essence and your courage, and it wouldn't hurt to bring a fire blanket."],
"town.alchemist.intro": ["I'm Auntie Alembic, dear heart, alchemist and keeper of some very nervous glassware, so please don't touch anything. ...Oh, go on then, you may touch that one. It likes you.","When you collect more copies of a card than you can carry, dear heart, the extras boil down into essence of that card's Path. Nothing goes to waste here, which is how I like a kitchen and a kingdom.","Bring me six essence each of two Paths, plus 100 gold, and I'll brew you a card of both. The cauldron picks which card, and now and then it's on fire. I only take what the brew needs; the rest stays in your jars.","Your jars hold eighteen of a Path. Anything past that drifts off as steam, and then my ceiling turns a new colour and I have to pretend I meant it.","They say there was one spring once, the Wellspring, that fed all four Paths, and everything mixed at the source. Everything's better mixed, dear heart. That is the kingdom I brew for."],
"town.alchemist.return": ["Six essence each of two Paths and 100 gold, dear heart, and the cauldron does the rest. Do lower your voice near the red flask, though, because it takes things very personally."],
"town.alchemist.quest_gift": ["Oh, and here, before I drift off and forget: a starter jar of every Path, six of each, which is enough for one brew of any two. Please don't drink it, dear heart. People do drink it."],
"town.alchemist.need_more": ["You don't have enough essence of two different Paths yet, dear heart. Collect more duplicates and then come back to me, and the cauldron and I will wait.", "The cauldron is very patient, bless it. Just please don't mistake its being patient for its having had lunch."],
"zone.complete.beefcake.title": ["THE GAINLANDS ARE FREE!"],
"zone.complete.beefcake.body": ["Chancellor Clench is down, Grandmaster Flex is back, and the weights are in the gym. The mills turn at a sensible pace; Gary lifts with a spotter."],
"zone.complete.gourmand.title": ["THE ENDLESS BUFFET IS FREE!"],
"zone.complete.gourmand.body": ["The Doppelganger is exposed, the Special Sauce is recalled, and the real Grand Chef is back in her own kitchen with the golems guarding plates again. Nobody leaves hungry."],
"zone.complete.necrocrat.title": ["THE D.N.A. IS FREE!"],
"zone.complete.necrocrat.body": ["Mortimer Grimsby is removed from office, and the vacancy passes by policy to the senior-most applicant on file: Agnes Overdue. The Department of Necrotic Affairs belongs to itself again, and it is terrified by the freedom."],
"zone.complete.refusemancer.title": ["THE VERDANT DUMP IS FREE!"],
"zone.complete.refusemancer.body": ["The Rotheart has gone silent and the vines are only vines again. The Archdruid is herself once more, deeply apologetic about the barn, and slowly the land begins to heal."],
"zone.complete.count": ["%d of 4 zones free"],
"town.objective": ["{villain} rules the four Paths through his rulers. Beat each road's gatekeeper, then free its zone by beating the boss of its main dungeon.","The imperial road to the Capital is open from the start, but its broken services will flatten you. Free the zones first. Gatekeeper Brannoch can explain."],
"town.objective.free": ["All four Paths are free. Buy cards, test yourself in the Undercroft, and brew something dangerous at the Alchemist's."],
"town.elder.postgame": ["{villain} is gone, and the Paths are out in the street shouting at one another again. I have never in my life been so glad to be annoyed.", "The Capital is open to everyone now, and your decks may mix any Paths you like. Go and see what you can make of it all, dearie. Then come home and eat."],
"town.objective.postgame": ["{villain} has fallen and the Paths are free to mix. Build decks from three or four Paths at once, try the Alchemist's tri-Path crafting, test yourself in the Undercroft and visit the changed Capital."],
"town.arena.unlock_line": ["Something under the old cottage at the end of Champions' Road is open for business. Listen for the crowd."],
"town.alchemist.unlock_line": ["Auntie Alembic's, the Alchemist, is now open in {town}. Bring your leftovers."],
"town.pack_vendor.name": ["Foil Fenwick"],
"town.pack_vendor.title": ["Fenwick's Sealed Goods"],
"town.pack_vendor.first": ["Psst... do you hear that crinkle? That's possibility, that is, with excellent packaging.", "I'm Foil Fenwick, Purveyor of Sealed Goods, and I sell packs and only packs. Open yours where the light's good, would you... if I cry, I'd like to see what I'm crying about.", "Here's how it works... whenever a Path's final dungeon falls, that Path sends me its pack. Don't ask me how. There's a great deal of foil and no paperwork at all, which the Necrocrats find very upsetting.", "Free a zone and I'll stock its pack, and until then it's only a rumour in a wrapper. Browse all you like, and sniff them if you want to... I won't judge you. I sniff them too."],
"town.pack_vendor.return": ["Browse, sniff, but please don't shake the packs... well, a little, then, if you must. I'm a collector, you see, and not a strong person.", "A repeat customer... shh, listen to that foil. I think you understand me, and I honestly don't know what to do with that."],
"town.pack_vendor.prismatic_reveal": ["Fenwick draws a curtain aside, very gently. \"This is the back room... Prismatic packs, with every Path in one wrapper.\"", "\"They only exist because the Paths are talking to each other again, which is terrible for my exclusivity... and quite wonderful for my sales.\""],
"pack.vendor.bought": ["Crinkle! You've made a wrapper very happy.", "Sealed, signed, and slightly warm.", "No refunds on bad luck. Bad luck is non-transferable.", "It wants to be opened. I'm trying to respect its wishes without getting involved."],
"pack.vendor.poor": ["Gold, friend. The foil does not accept good intentions.", "Not enough gold. The wrapper can tell."],
"pack.vendor.locked": ["Not yet. That one is still a rumour in a wrapper."],
"town.tailor.name": ["Pip Threadwell"],
"town.tailor.title": ["Threadwell's Hats & Hems"],
"town.tailor.line": ["Look closely, do, because every stitch tells a story, and the very best of them tell it with a feather."],
"town.tailor.first": ["A hat! You need a hat, on that marvellous head. Now hold still, please: your left shoulder is a size braver than your right, and I'd hate to flatter the wrong one.", "I am Pip Threadwell, Haberdasher and Hemmer! Everything in here is purely cosmetic, I must confess, and it will not make you stronger, braver or better at card games.", "It will, however, make you LOOK all three, and I maintain that is eighty percent of the job. Do try anything on in the little mirror first: hats up top, cloaks down the back, and dye on both.", "Free zones and climb levels, and I shall find you grander stock. I hear rumours of rarer pieces too, because people will tell a hatmaker everything while he's pinning them."],
"town.tailor.return": ["Back to change your mind and your hat, are we? Excellent, because one of those I can fit properly, and the other I shall simply admire.", "My favourite head, and in the nick of time! Is it to be brim, brooch or something billowing? I ask because this could very well be a hem-ergency."],
"town.tailor.progress": ["Oh, you have been busy, and so have I, because new fabrics have arrived. Please don't ask me where from. Some of them were yelling when I unrolled them.", "My stock has grown! The freed zones send me their finest fashions, slightly singed and mostly fabulous, and I mend the singed ones gladly, because a patch is the strongest part of a coat."],
"town.tailor.secrets": ["Between us: a crown made of living leaves is growing in a bin somewhere in the Verdant Dump, and a cloak that has survived more than you have is draped over a chest on a muscly island.", "And as for the Capital's mantle... well, someone would have to defeat its owner first, and that is no small fitting. The mantle, frankly, is rooting for you."],
"tailor.bought": ["Gorgeous. Truly. You are going to turn heads, mostly in confusion.", "Wear it out! A hat cannot have an entrance if you keep it in a bag!", "Sold! Such a dramatic fit - the hat looks surprised to be wearing you."],
"tailor.poor": ["Gold, my dear head. Thread is not free, and neither is my charm.", "A little more gold, my dear head. I can work wonders with fabric, but it insists on being paid for."],
"tailor.locked": ["Not yet. That one is still on the sewing table, and it is sulking."],
"tailor.equipped": ["Hat! On the head, where hats belong. My work here is done. Briefly.", "A classic. Wear it like you mean it, and tilt it a fraction left. Your left. No, my left. Perfect."],
"tailor.bare_head": ["No hat. Bold. Brave. Wrong, but brave.", "The bare-head look! I shall lie down in the back for a moment. Carry on."],
"tailor.owned": ["You own that one already! Do introduce it to the outside world."],
"tailor.plain_cloak": ["The Plain Cloak, undyed! Classic. Humble. Secretly the best cut in the shop. I made it, so I would know."],
"tailor.dyed": ["A new colour! Hold still while the cloak gets used to it. Gasp. It suits you. It suits it.", "Dyed and dried! Walk into the light. No, more light. There. Devastating."],
"tailor.cloak_on": ["Cloak! Over the shoulders, swishing on cue. Do turn around once. For me.", "A cloak with a past. You will give it a future. Mind the hem on stairs."],
"pack.hint.path_beefcake": ["Stocked once the Gainlands' final dungeon is cleared."],
"pack.hint.path_gourmand": ["Stocked once the Endless Buffet's final dungeon is cleared."],
"pack.hint.path_refusemancer": ["Stocked once the Verdant Dump's final dungeon is cleared."],
"pack.hint.path_necrocrat": ["Stocked once the D.N.A.'s final dungeon is cleared."],
"pack.hint.gilded_beefcake": ["Fig can only get these once the Gainlands are free."],
"pack.hint.gilded_gourmand": ["Fig can only get these once the Endless Buffet is free."],
"pack.hint.gilded_refusemancer": ["Fig can only get these once the Verdant Dump is free."],
"pack.hint.gilded_necrocrat": ["Fig can only get these once the D.N.A. is free."],
"pack.hint.general_2": ["The back crates open at level 10, or once two zones are free, whichever comes first."],
"pack.hint.prismatic": ["Unlocks after the final victory."],
"pack.card_vendor.title": ["Sable's Sealed Surprises"],
"pack.card_vendor.line": ["Sable pats a stack of wrapped bundles. \"Surprise packs, darling, fresh from the crates, and I make it a rule never to ask a crate where it has been.\"", "\"What's inside them? I did ask, darling, but the crate declined to comment, and I do admire a professional.\""],
"pack.card_vendor.tier2": ["Sable grins at you. \"The back crates are open at last, darling, with more cards and bigger surprises, and the same discreet policy on fainting as before.\""],
"pack.black_market.title": ["Fig's Gilded Goods"],
"pack.black_market.line": ["Fig Sly taps a gold-edged wrapper. \"Guaranteed good stuff. Do not ask where the guarantee comes from.", "It is not legal. It is, however, very shiny.\""],
"pack.reward.clear": ["The Path sends you its pack: %s."],
"pack.reward.first_bonus": ["First clear bonus: %s."],
"pack.reward.vendor_unlock": ["Foil Fenwick now stocks the %s."],
"pack.reward.title": ["Packs received"],
"pack.reward.primm": ["Every Path sends a thank-you: %s."],
"pack.reward.quest": ["Pack reward: %s."],
"arena.tier.1": ["Bronze Sand"],
"arena.tier.2": ["Silver Sand"],
"arena.tier.3": ["Gold Sand"],
"arena.tier.1.blurb": ["Where every champion starts: loud, dusty and mostly forgiving."],
"arena.tier.2.blurb": ["The crowd has stopped laughing and started betting."],
"arena.tier.3.blurb": ["Only legends stand here. Only the sand remembers who fell."],
"arena.arena_warmup.title": ["Warm-Up Brawl"],
"arena.arena_warmup.blurb": ["A rookie gladiator rattles inside oversized armor. Bring your own deck; the armor has enough room for its own audience."],
"arena.arena_warmup.rules": ["Your own deck, full HP. Win the duel."],
"arena.arena_lethal_lunch.title": ["Lethal Lunch"],
"arena.arena_lethal_lunch.blurb": ["The lunch rush has an enemy blocker, ten HP and no mercy. You have exactly one turn and just enough energy."],
"arena.arena_lethal_lunch.rules": ["PUZZLE: win THIS turn. Preset board. If the turn ends and your opponent still stands, you lose."],
"arena.arena_neutral_mile.title": ["The Neutral Mile"],
"arena.arena_neutral_mile.blurb": ["The Marshal's favorite warm-down: no Paths, no tricks, no excuses. Everyone fights with a borrowed gladiator's kit."],
"arena.arena_neutral_mile.rules": ["RESTRICTED DECK: you fight with the Gladiator's Kit (neutral cards), not your own deck."],
"arena.arena_hold_the_line.title": ["Hold the Line"],
"arena.arena_hold_the_line.blurb": ["A stampeding squad charges across the sand before you can even take a breath. You only have to outlast them."],
"arena.arena_hold_the_line.rules": ["PUZZLE: survive 3 of the enemy's turns. Preset board; the enemy moves first. You win when the third enemy turn ends and you still stand."],
"arena.arena_spells_only.title": ["Spells Only, Please"],
"arena.arena_spells_only.blurb": ["The Cardboard Colossus does not like being hit by anything with a heartbeat. Win without playing a single unit."],
"arena.arena_spells_only.rules": ["RESTRICTED DECK + RULE: you fight with the Spellslinger's Satchel and may NOT play unit cards this duel."],
"arena.arena_four_fists.title": ["The Four Fists"],
"arena.arena_four_fists.blurb": ["A champion who fights with every Path at once, and has a fist for each. Bring your best deck."],
"arena.arena_four_fists.rules": ["Your own deck, full HP. Win the duel."],
"arena.arena_zero_to_hero.title": ["Zero to Hero"],
"arena.arena_zero_to_hero.blurb": ["The Wall of Fame has two blockers and eleven HP. The crowd has already booked your funeral. Show them lethal."],
"arena.arena_zero_to_hero.rules": ["PUZZLE: win THIS turn. Preset board, five energy, two blockers to deal with."],
"arena.arena_marshal.title": ["The Marshal"],
"arena.arena_marshal.blurb": ["Announcer Grand Bellows steps onto the sand. He has not lost a bout in eleven years. He is smiling, and so is the moustache."],
"arena.arena_marshal.rules": ["Your own deck, full HP. Win the duel. No excuses."],
"arena.screen.title": ["The Undercroft"],
"arena.screen.locked": ["The gates are chained until the first zone is free."],
"arena.screen.cleared": ["CLEARED"],
"arena.screen.new": ["NEW"],
"arena.screen.replay": ["Replay (no prize)"],
"arena.screen.fight": ["Fight"],
"arena.screen.first_prize": ["First-clear prize"],
"arena.screen.puzzle": ["PUZZLE"],
"arena.screen.battle": ["BATTLE"],
"arena.won.first": ["VICTORY ON THE SAND, AND THE PRIZE IS YOURS! (normal voice) Do mind your head on the way up to collect it, because the ceiling doesn't celebrate with the rest of us."],
"arena.won.replay": ["ANOTHER WIN FOR THE BOOKS! (normal voice) Here are a few coins from the crowd. The crowd is only me, I know, but I mean every one of them."],
"arena.lost": ["NOT THIS TIME, CHAMPION! (normal voice) Come back whenever you're ready, there's no hurry at all, and between ourselves the sand has yet to win a rematch."],
"arena.puzzle.won": ["PUZZLE SOLVED - THE CROWD GOES WILD! (normal voice) Lovely bit of thinking, that. I could hear the gears turning from the booth."],
"arena.puzzle.lost": ["THE PUZZLE WINS THIS ROUND! (normal voice) Have a good long look at the board and try again. It's not going anywhere, and neither am I."],
"travel.title": ["The Beefcake Rift Express"],
"travel.subtitle": ["Rips while-you-wait. Tips accepted in protein."],
"travel.here": ["You are here. A Rip is stationed here."],
"travel.locked.name": ["???"],
"travel.locked.blurb": ["No station yet. Walk into that town yourself and a cousin will turn up and rip one into the nearest wall."],
"travel.warning": ["Ripping out of a zone ends your visit: you arrive at full HP, and the roaming enemies there come back. Rips are free, and so is the spotting."],
"travel.button": ["Rip me there!"],
"travel.close": ["Not today"],
"travel.operator.town": ["Rip Tearson, Rift Technician"],
"travel.operator.necrocrat": ["Rip Tearson (Cousin #2)"],
"travel.operator.beefcake": ["Rip Tearson (Cousin #3)"],
"travel.operator.gourmand": ["Rip Tearson (Cousin #4, the One Who Eats)"],
"travel.operator.refusemancer": ["Rip Tearson (Cousin #5, Smells Fine)"],
"travel.operator.final": ["Rip Tearson (Cousin #7, Allegedly)"],
"travel.station.town.name": ["{town}"],
"travel.station.town.blurb": ["The home station. A well-supported sky is a happy sky."],
"travel.station.necrocrat.name": ["The Department of Necrotic Affairs"],
"travel.station.necrocrat.blurb": ["The elevator lobby, where a cousin ripped it into the wall beside the Out-Of-Order sign. It's the only thing in the building that works."],
"travel.station.beefcake.name": ["The Gainlands: Swole Station"],
"travel.station.beefcake.blurb": ["Between the hot tub and the protein stand, where the gains are public."],
"travel.station.gourmand.name": ["The Endless Buffet: The Grand Pantry"],
"travel.station.gourmand.blurb": ["A short walk from the heavy meal table. The cousin ripped it open right by the napkins, so you'll never arrive without one."],
"travel.station.refusemancer.name": ["The Verdant Dump: The Compost Grange"],
"travel.station.refusemancer.blurb": ["Right by the harvest table. The Rip on duty is slightly damp, but then so is everything else out there."],
"travel.station.final.name": ["{capital}: The Crease"],
"travel.station.final.blurb": ["A rip into the hideout under the Capital. Don't ask how we found it; we followed the smell of Fig Sly's hot sauce straight through the fabric of space."],
"travel.intro.town": ["HNNNGH. SPOTTER! Spot me! No, not you, the other guy. ...Oh, hello there, and welcome to the Beefcake Rift Express.", "We tear the world open so you don't have to walk, buddy. It takes two men to hold the sky up while you go through, and that's what we call our overhead.", "The sky is heavier than it looks, buddy, which is why we never skip sky day. Do not look at the seam. It's working very hard, and it's shy about being watched.", "Reach a new town and we'll send a cousin to rip a station there. Every one of them is called Rip, because our mother found a name she liked and saw no reason to stop.", "After that, you can rip between any two stations whenever you like. Thank you for ripping with the Express, and please keep your elbows inside the sky."],
"travel.return.town": ["Back for another rip, buddy? Just say where and we'll tear it right open for you. Rips are free, same as always.", "Spotting is free too, buddy. Water, I'm sorry to say, you'll have to bring yourself, because we get through all of ours."],
"travel.intro.zone": ["HNNNGH... Rip Tearson, Beefcake Rift Express, proudly serving this exact spot. I'm one of the cousins, and I'm happy to say we hire entirely on relative strength.", "We're all very proud of one another, the whole family, and we show it by rarely speaking.", "So just say where you're headed, buddy, and we'll rip it for you."],
"travel.return.zone": ["Need a rip, buddy? I've been holding this sky since breakfast, and I'd hate to put it down without anyone going through it."],
"travel.intro.final": ["Shhh, keep it down, buddy, there's a Wrinkle asleep behind the crates. I'm Rip Tearson, Cousin Number Seven, Rift Express. Allegedly.", "They told me this place didn't exist, so I went ahead and ripped a hole to it anyway, because sometimes you just have to believe in yourself. The sauce smell helped a lot too."],
"travel.rip.1": ["Grab the edges! On three! One!", "...Two! ...What comes after two? ...RIP!"],
"travel.rip.2": ["Hold the sky, brother! Feel the burn! RRRRRIP!"],
"travel.rip.3": ["Spot this whole dimension, brother! Lift with your LEGS! Nobody ever tore the sky open with their lower back!"],
"travel.rip.4": ["Loosen the shoulders, roll the neck, and tear a hole in the fabric of space. And never, ever skip leg day, brother."],
"travel.rip.sound": ["RIIIIIIP!"],
"travel.arrive.town": ["The rift folds shut behind you with a very satisfied pop. A nearby Beefcake flexes at the hole to say well done."],
"travel.arrive.necrocrat": ["The rift drops you by the lobby elevator and pops shut. You catch a fluttering memo: YOU WERE NOT AUTHORIZED TO ARRIVE.", "You turn the memo over, looking for an approved way to have arrived. There isn't one."],
"travel.arrive.beefcake": ["The rift spits you out next to the Swole Station. A passing brute gives you a thumbs-up, then another to himself, then one to the hole."],
"travel.arrive.gourmand": ["You land in the Pantry, and someone hands you a napkin before you've found your feet."],
"travel.arrive.refusemancer": ["You arrive at the Grange in a whiff of ozone, mulch and gym sock, and the gym sock is definitely the Express."],
"travel.arrive.final": ["The rift spits you out in the Crease. Somebody says shh. Somebody else says it was not them. The rift closes politely."],
"travel.unlock.title": ["Rift Station ripped"],
"travel.unlock.toast": ["A Beefcake cousin has ripped a Rift Station into this town. Fast travel unlocked."],
"travel.unlock.necrocrat": ["Rift Station unlocked: the Department of Necrotic Affairs. A cousin ripped it in beside the Out-Of-Order sign. Fast travel to and from here is now open."],
"travel.unlock.beefcake": ["Rift Station unlocked: the Gainlands. Two cousins have ripped it in with their bare hands and are now doing a victory pose. Fast travel to and from here is now open."],
"travel.unlock.gourmand": ["Rift Station unlocked: the Endless Buffet. A cousin ripped it in, then asked if there were seconds. Fast travel to and from here is now open."],
"travel.unlock.refusemancer": ["Rift Station unlocked: the Verdant Dump. A cousin ripped it in, then looked at his hands, then at the hole, then at his hands again. Fast travel to and from here is now open."],
"travel.unlock.final": ["Rift Station unlocked: the Crease, the hideout under the Capital. A very quiet cousin ripped it in. Fast travel to and from here is now open."],
"travel.prompt": ["Use the Rift Station"],
"travel.sign.town": ["BEEFCAKE RIFT EXPRESS", "Rips while-you-wait. Space torn to order. No refunds on the sky."],
"travel.sign.zone": ["BEEFCAKE RIFT EXPRESS", "A cousin is on duty. Do not look at the seam."],
"travel.station.forest.name": ["The Forest Outside {town}"],
"travel.station.forest.blurb": ["A hasty rip between the trees where you first woke up. There's a hatch south of the clearing now that nobody remembers being there, and it smells like a hospital."],
"travel.operator.forest": ["Rip Tearson (Cousin #8, Mossy)"],
"travel.sign.forest": ["BEEFCAKE RIFT EXPRESS", "FOREST STATION", "(Please do not eat the hatch.)"],
"travel.intro.forest": ["HNNNGH. Rip Tearson, Cousin Number Eight, rift technician and tree enthusiast. This is where I found the hatch, buddy, and no, before you ask, I didn't open it.", "I've got manners, mostly, and my mother would hear about it if I hadn't.", "Say the word and I'll rip you back to {town}. Or if you're going down the hatch, I'll hold the sky open right here till you're back up."],
"travel.return.forest": ["Back to {town}, buddy, or down the hatch? Either way, I've been holding this sky since breakfast and it's ready when you are."],
"travel.arrive.forest": ["Forest station! Mind the roots. And the hatch. Mostly the hatch."],
"travel.forest_tip": ["Spotter! I've got big news. You know that forest outside town, the one where you first turned up?", "I went up there on my day off and saw some very interesting things. The brambles south of the clearing just... let go, and there's a path now, with a hatch at the end that was NOT there before. Glowing roots, and a hospital smell.", "I didn't open it, because I have manners, and also because I'm scared. But I did put a rift station up there, so you can pop over whenever you like.", "It's on the Express now, so come to any of my stations and say 'forest', and I'll tear it right open for you.", "Maren says that's where they took your friend from the castle gate. I'd go down myself, but it feels like yours to open. Be careful, buddy."],
"postgame.rescuer.freed": ["You came back for me. Down there, on purpose. I'm going to need a while to stop being cross about it.", "Go and finish it, Tess. I'll be here when you come up, and I've had a great deal of practice at waiting in this forest."],
"postgame.rescuer.cleared": ["The Lab is quiet now, and for the first time in ten years I can hear the trees from down there.", "Dad is in {town}, listening to Maren. She let him have one slice of pie and no more, and I've never seen him so frightened of anything."],
"travel.unlock.forest": ["Rift Station unlocked: the forest outside {town}. Rip has torn it open where you first woke up. Fast travel to and from here is now open."],
}
